Razorpay & PhonePe Fintech Application – Manual Testing
Project Overview
This project demonstrates manual testing performed on UPI / Digital Payments & Fintech applications (Razorpay & PhonePe sandbox).
The objective was to validate money movement, transaction integrity, duplicate prevention, authentication, refunds, and usability across critical workflows.

Application Under Test
Application: Razorpay & PhonePe Fintech App (Sandbox)
Technology: UPI / Digital Payments Platform
Testing Type: Manual Testing

Testing Performed
Smoke Testing – Critical login and transaction flows

Sanity Testing – Verification of specific fixes and targeted features

Functional Testing – Add money, send/receive, QR scan-to-pay, refunds, history

Boundary Testing – Limits, precision, minimum/maximum values

Negative Testing – Invalid inputs, duplicate attempts, blocked senders

Resilience & Recovery Testing – Network drops, app kill/reopen, retries

Usability & Privacy Testing – Error messages, masking, confirmation clarity

Compatibility Testing – Android/iOS versions, browsers, screen sizes

Test Documentation
The Excel workbook contains the following documentation:

RTM (Requirements Traceability Matrix) – Mapping requirements to test cases

Detailed Test Cases – 200+ cases across modules

Bug Log – Severity/Priority defect records

Exploratory Charters – Session-based exploratory notes

Test Data Sheets – Synthetic data for safe execution

Resume Highlights – Project summary for portfolio

